<title>CANADA: Quebec sets C$350 million bond due April, 2026.</title>
<headline>Quebec sets C$350 million bond due April, 2026.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Province of Quebec on Wednesday set C$350 million of 8.5 percent bonds due April 1, 2026 in financial markets, said lead manager Levesque Beaubien Geoffrion.  </p>
<p>The bond was priced at C$114.843 to yield 7.262 percent, 40 basis points over the Government of Canada's 8.0 percent bond due June, 2023.</p>
<p>The issue will be delivered on June 16, 1997.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
